shape theory.fixed-point : theory.distinguishing-character, theory.self-reference {
  type: theorem
  layer: 0
  """
// Theorem 4.2 (Fixed Point of the Minimal Shape).
// A shape with no distinguishing character beyond self-reference is
// a fixed point of its own transformation: M' = M.
//
// Let B be such a shape. Its character references only its own prior
// character, and that character has no content beyond the reference
// itself. Suppose M' includes content X that M lacks. Then B has
// character beyond self-reference, contradicting the premise. Suppose
// X is transient: then B has the dynamical pattern of generating and
// removing X, which is itself distinguishing character. Therefore no
// new content can appear, even transiently. M' = M.
//
// Derives from: theory.distinguishing-character,
//               theory.self-reference
  """
}
